<title>PAKISTAN: Member removed from two Pakistani stock exchanges.</title>
<headline>Member removed from two Pakistani stock exchanges.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Corporate Law Authority (CLA) has cancelled the membership of Zafar Moti in the Karachi and Lahore stock exchanges on the charge of violating trading laws, a CLA official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The membership of Zafar Moti has been removed from both the exchanges with immediate effect for violating trading laws,&quot; a CLA spokesman told Reuters by telephone from Islamabad. &quot;He did not hand over shares bought and proceeds of shares sold to an investor.&quot;</p>
<p>Moti was not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
